(c) 2022 Charles Marsh. Its source commit is
05cdc36a45a29e078c2af9358969d0f576408bef. The complete upstream license,
including its retained third-party notices, is in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ruff-LICENSE.txt.

Configuration/kind/routing snapshots, native argument constraints, name checks,
YAML policy and Jinja formatting compatibility were compared with/adapted from
the pinned ansible-lint and ansible-core sources identified above. The executable
contains Rust implementations and declarative snapshots; it does not embed or
launch the upstream Python implementations. Development-only metadata generation
and differential comparison scripts require the reference Python environment.

Installed collection metadata support (2026-10-31)
------------------------------------------------
Native metadata reading uses static Python AST and YAML analysis. The embedded
documentation-fragment, common file-option and action-plugin snapshots derive
from the pinned ansible-core version above (GPL-3.0-or-later). Scalar/list/dict
coercion and action-plugin precedence were compared with its common validation
utilities and the pinned ansible-lint args rule. Installed collection source is
read locally and is not copied into release archives.
